SUMMARY:Baobab: A Percussion-filled Fable
DESCRIPTION:The djembe drums dance and the ngoni’s strings sing as the griots tell a tale passed down from generation to generation. Long ago\, when the stars were still babies\, the trees and animals talked\, and a water-stealing sun burned overhead\, a baobab tree bore an unexpected and unusual gift. Featuring music from Mali and Senegal\, puppets large and small\, one naughty monkey\, and a witch with an itch to dance\, Baobab is a percussion-filled fable about a boy’s heroic quest to save his village from drought. \n\nAt 6 pm in the lobby\, enjoy free children’s activities\, dancing from Imani Edu-tainers\, and small bites of African food from Upohar World Kitchen! \n            \n        \n                \n                \n    Learn More
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/baobab-a-percussion-filled-fable/
LOCATION:Ware Center for the Arts\, 42 N. Prince St.\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Arts & Entertainment
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2025/10/Baobab.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="Millersville University Office of Visual & Performing Arts":MAILTO:cori.jackson@millersville.edu
END:VEVENT
