SUMMARY:SOUL & SPIRIT A Gospel • Jazz • Spoken Word Experience
DESCRIPTION:First Reformed Church of Lancaster will present Soul & Spirit\, a sacred arts experience celebrating Black history\, faith\, resilience\, justice\, and hope through Gospel music\, Jazz\, and the Spoken Word on Sunday\, May 3 at 4 PM in their historic 1854 sanctuary at 40 E. Orange Street in downtown Lancaster.  Soul & Spirit is not a traditional concert—it is worship through art. Through sound and story\, the program honors the past\, speaks truth to the present\, and imagines a hopeful future. Originally scheduled in February to honor Black History month\, the event was postponed due to winter storms.  \nHosted by Dr. Dominique Denman\, Soul & Spirit invites the community into a meaningful Black History Month celebration rooted in faith\, creativity\, and collective memory.  The program also features Dr. Kellie Turner\, and Ms. Alanna Piper.\nAll are warmly invited to experience Soul & Spirit where you can expect a 90-minute curated sacred arts program of Gospel music\, Jazz\, and Spoken Word performances\, a welcoming\, reflective\, and celebratory atmosphere with a diverse audience from across the Lancaster community.\nCome as you are. Bring your spirit.  Leave inspired.\nThis event is free and open to the public. A freewill offering will be received during the program to support the ongoing care\, repair\, and sustainability of First Reformed Lancaster’s historic sacred space. \n            \n        \n                \n                \n    Learn More
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/soul-spirit-a-gospel-jazz-spoken-word-experience-2/
LOCATION:First Reformed Church\, 40 East Orange Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17602\, United States
CATEGORIES:Arts & Entertainment
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/04/Dr-Domi-1-2026.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="First Reformed Church":MAILTO:webmaster.FRCLancaster@gmail.com
END:VEVENT
